cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use biohttp in your work, please cite it as below.
title: "biohttp: Normalized HTTP Transport with Circuit Breaking and Caching"
abstract: >-
  An HTTP transport layer for R clients of web services. Calls return a
  normalized result value rather than raising a condition, so transport
  failure, a non-success status code, and an unreadable response body are
  three distinct outcomes a caller can branch on. Per-host circuit breaking,
  retry, throttling, header redaction, and a success-only cache are provided
  as defaults.
type: software
version: 0.1.0
